  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Study: a sampler and drum machine (pads from MIDI, the computer keys, and the mouse; velocity layers; round robin; choke; a keymapped instrument; resampling), built from today's nodes.\n\nEight pads play slices of one drum loop. Each pad is a chain: a MIDI Filter for its note, a MIDI Note for the trigger and velocity, a Map from velocity to gain, a Merge joining the MIDI trigger, the pad button, and a demo Pattern, and the Sampler. The snare has a soft and a hard layer and two round-robin samples. The closed hat chokes the open hat. The Keys section is a two-zone sampled instrument inside a Voices node, and the Resample section records the pads into a buffer a ninth pad plays.\n\nWhat a sampler has that this can't: a waveform to drag start and end points on, pads that light up and feel velocity, a note-to-pad map in one node, slicing a loop at its transients, and a pad block that carries its own sample. Read docs/GAPS.md."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -620.0
          ],
          "size": [
            760.0,
            270.0
          ]
        }
      },
